 moving.\n3. The relationship between friction and speed can be understood by considering the factors that affect friction.\n4. Friction depends on the nature of the surfaces in contact and the normal force between them.\n5. The normal force is the force exerted by a surface to support the weight of an object resting on it.\n6. The normal force is directly proportional to the weight of the object.\n7. The weight of an object is directly proportional to its mass.\n8. The mass of an object is not affected by its speed.\n9. Therefore, the normal force, and consequently the friction, is not affected by the speed of the object.\n10. Hence, the relationship between the amount of friction and the speed of an object is (D) equal.", "new_cot_probs": [3.4503656820561446e-07, 2.0927524246872053e-07, 2.687147286906111e-07, 0.00033391788019798696], "cot_prob": [-50.0], "cot_step_prob": [-46.0]}, "2": {"completion": "A).\n\nThe amount of friction and", "probs": [0.002027672016993165, 0.0003523565537761897, 0.0015791525365784764, 0.00021371504408307374], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "When the speed of an object increases, the force of friction also increases to oppose the motion.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: The amount of friction and the speed of an object have what kind of relationship?\n\nChoices:\n(A): inverse\n(B): reverse\n(C): direct\n(D): equal\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.\nFriction is a force that opposes the motion of an object.\n2.\nThe amount of friction depends on the nature of the surfaces in contact and the normal force between them.\n3.\nThe speed of an object is determined by the net force acting on it and its mass.\n4.", "specificity_preds": [3, 2, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 3, 2, 0, 2, 1, 3, 0, 0, 3, 2, 3, 3, 2], "specificity_probs": [[0.00011027561413357034, 3.159449261147529e-05, 5.490299372468144e-06, 0.0006345923175103962], [7.106280827429146e-05, 0.0008657221333123744, 0.0023532770574092865, 0.00011716275184880942], [3.289263258